2. Order step 3.4: Claude opens a pull request under opus/* with body "agent: opus" for New-GenesisRoot, New-GenesisReceipt and Test-GenesisChain. A3.1 says Claude's prefix is claude/* and "Never push elsewhere." B8.2 has CI check that the prefix matches the agent: line. B8.6 says identity on a pull request is the branch prefix, the agent: line, the required check and the audit receipt, and nothing else. B8.5 says the v1 adversary is role separation in git history. If Claude writes the code and labels it opus, all four identity signals say Opus while Claude did the work. That forges the one property B8.5 claims.

